      "role": "user",
      "content": "that's super dark and exactly what the character would say. so if you were to put this into a formal historical argument—not just for the novel, but like, if someone were actually arguing this in a debate—would you say that most historians are just being too simplistic by focusing on the economics? like, is the \"people-driven\" narrative basically just a way to avoid looking at how much control a single figure can actually exert?",
